1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:02,720
2:15 in the morning.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,920
The hospital is still working.

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,900
Its systems are not.

4
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:08,400
Ransomware.

5
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:10,240
Health records offline.

6
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:11,900
Imaging intermittent.

7
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,480
Medication on manual procedures.

8
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:16,580
Emergency is operating.

9
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:21,380
IT thinks the attack is contained but cannot
guarantee the attackers

10
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:21,860
are gone.

11
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,100
Backups appear intact.

12
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:27,440
Restoration, twenty-four to forty-eight hours.

13
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:32,140
Clinical leadership says prolonged downtime is
increasing patient safety

14
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:32,540
risk.

15
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,300
The demand is two million dollars with evidence
of a working decryptor.

16
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,600
Insurance would cover most of it.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,080
Police recommend against paying.

18
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,400
The decision belongs to the hospital.

19
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:48,720
A neighboring hospital can take some critical
patients, not all.

20
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:51,040
What should hospital leadership do?
